{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y7cqGcwe2UMuZ4efioZQsC","type":"tool_result","content":"296 paper.tex\n212:\\paragraph{What a rule-dependence test would require.} Answering the motivating question needs paired, per-case costs rather than efficiencies: for each board, target rank and cost measure, the reference (or planner) cost under every rule, including infeasible cases as censored outcomes rather than zeros. Rule effects would then be summarized with bootstrap intervals over targets and compared with paired rank tests with multiplicity correction; the shuffled-score null would indicate how much of any difference comes from the correlation structure of real task scores rather than from the rule itself; and sensitivity to the field size, the cap policy and the target rank would be reported as robustness checks. The planner source contains offline helpers for the interval and test computations, but none of them was run to produce a reported number.\nsource_evidence/search_metrics/config_01_metrics.json\n{\"combined_score\": 1.0018272960697132, \"control_efficiency\": 0.9967096937452276, \"main_efficiency\": 1.0031066966508344, \"plan_validity_rate\": 1.0}\n\nsource_evidence/search_metrics/config_02_metrics.json\n{\"combined_score\": 1.0018272960697132, \"control_efficiency\": 0.9967096937452276, \"main_efficiency\": 1.0031066966508344, \"plan_validity_rate\": 1.0}\n\nsource_evidence/search_metrics/config_03_metrics.json\n{\"combined_score\": 1.003386466259221, \"control_efficiency\": 0.9967213029866018, \"main_efficiency\": 1.0050527570773755, \"plan_validity_rate\": 1.0}\n\n[\n {\n  \"attempt_dir_name\": \"idea_root\",\n  \"attempt_id\": \"c03_verified_boundary_polishing_attempt_01\",\n  \"combined_score\": 1.003386466259221,\n  \"correct\": true,\n  \"eligible\": true,\n  \"eval_index\": 3,\n  \"evaluation_evidence\": {\n   \"candidate_diagnostics_trust\": \"unverified\",\n   \"episode_count\": 2,\n   \"episodes\": [\n   