l plane raw files, rows and columns, plus seed and split manifests\",\n136:\\paragraph{Data and splits.} Development uses the 57 HELM MMLU v1.13.0 subject columns as tasks. The held-out evaluation uses two boards built from the Open LLM Leaderboard snapshots \\citep{OpenLLMLeaderboardContents2025}: a six-benchmark board from the \\texttt{contents} table and a sub-task-level board from the \\texttt{results} files for the same model pool, each restricted to the top $\\min(N,200)$ models. The evaluator verifies snapshot checksums and checks that the held-out boards are disjoint from the development data. Development seeds are 11 and 12; held-out seeds are 9001 and 9002.\n221:\\paragraph{Reproducibility statement.} The planner sources, the evaluator sources, the task contract and the script that builds each figure are included with the submission (Appendix~\\ref{app:repro}). Data snapshots are identified by revision hash and file checksums. All reported numbers are read from evaluator outputs.\n287:\\paragraph{Data.} Development: HELM MMLU release v1.13.0 (summary date 2025-01-10), 57 subject files, exact-match column, each file pinned by SHA-256 in the task manifest. Held-out: Open LLM Leaderboard \\texttt{contents} at revision \\texttt{9c09a7cae43334062a82cb164f2ef255013dafa2} (parquet SHA-256 \\texttt{f13a7061\\ldots dca5}) and \\texttt{results} at revision \\texttt{aa81ecc38fdc5708254b833923368970efdf5ef5} (derived sub-task file SHA-256 \\texttt{c4536f9f\\ldots 4a7f}). Flagged models and rows with missing values are excluded, and a newer submission replaces an older duplicate. Licenses: no dataset-level license is declared for the score data; the HELM code is Apache-2.0; \\texttt{contents} carries per-model Hub license fields. Use is limited to research analysis of published scores.\n{\n \"results\": [\n  {\n   \"locator\": \"final_evaluation.metrics.main_efficiency\",\n   \"messages\": [\n    \"Target path exists, but locator semantics were not interpreted by the b